---
import { trustPages } from "../data/trust-pages";
import TrustPageLayout from "../layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro";

const page = trustPages.editorialStandards;
---

<TrustPageLayout page={page} currentKey="editorialStandards">
  <h2>Start with a reader's decision</h2>
  <p>
    Each guide addresses a specific business problem and gives the reader a
    practical next step. Topics focus on choosing software, using AI and
    automation, protecting information, organizing work, and planning technology
    changes.
  </p>
  <h2>Sources and verification</h2>
  <p>
    Current official or primary sources are preferred for technical, regulatory,
    security, and platform claims. Analysis and decision tools are described as
    editorial synthesis when a source does not prescribe the exact method.
    Source access dates show when a reference was consulted. They are not a
    promise that a provider's features or terms remain unchanged. Link checks
    establish availability, not the accuracy of every claim.
  </p>
  <h2>Software comparisons and testing</h2>
  <p>
    Software comparisons use stated criteria tied to the business problem, such
    as implementation effort, training, integrations, data export, security,
    privacy, accessibility, support, total cost, and migration difficulty.
    Vendor material may establish documented capabilities, but it does not
    decide the editorial conclusion. Affiliate commission is never a comparison
    criterion.
  </p>
  <p>
    The publication does not describe a product as personally tested, assign an
    unsupported rating, or claim observed results unless a reproducible test
    actually occurred and its limits are documented. The current guides are
    source-checked, not represented as first-hand product testing. Worked
    examples are labeled as illustrations when their inputs are hypothetical.
  </p>
  <h2>Dates, updates, and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Publication and review dates reflect real editorial events, not an attempt
    to manufacture age or freshness. A modification date is used only for a
    substantive change; minor cleanup is not presented as a major update.
    Material corrections are handled under the <a href="/corrections/"
      >corrections process</a
    >.
  </p>
  <h2>Independence and commercial relationships</h2>
  <p>
    Advertising and affiliate links are currently inactive. Any future
    sponsorship or material conflict relevant to a guide must be disclosed
    clearly. Advertising, sponsorship, or affiliate relationships do not
    purchase favorable conclusions. Commercial arrangements remain separate from
    topic selection, sourcing, comparison criteria, and corrections. Current
    details appear in the <a href="/advertising-disclosure/"
      >advertising and affiliate disclosure</a
    >.
  </p>
  <h2 id="ai-assisted-workflow">AI-assisted workflow and responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    AI tools assisted these guides and this website with research organization,
    outlining, drafting, editing, and code generation. Sources, citations,
    claims, and generated code remain subject to verification; AI output is not
    treated as evidence merely because it was generated.
  </p>
  <p>
    A completed human editorial review of all guides has not been documented.
    The guides must not be read as expert-approved advice or firsthand product
    reviews. The owner remains responsible for editorial acceptance and for
    arranging any necessary privacy, legal, accessibility, or specialist review.
  </p>
</TrustPageLayout>
